 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new public water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 3622 Whites Creek Pike, also known as Whites Creek Estates (MWS Project Nos. 24-WL-47 and 24-SL-152 and Proposal No. 2026M-066ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 880 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 744 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 306 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), two fire hydrant assemblies, 11 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 3622 Whites Creek Pike, also known as Whites Creek Estates, is needed to construct project numbers 24-WL-47 and 24SL152; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M066ES-001 on July 24, 2026, for the acceptance of said water and sanitary sewer mains, fire hydrant assemblies, sanitary sewer manholes and easements.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 880 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 744 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 306 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), two fire hydrant assemblies, 11 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 3622 Whites Creek Pike, also known as Whites Creek Estates, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n04900010700\t\t\t\t\t3622 Whites Creek Pike\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance accepts approximately 880 linear feet of new eight-inch water main (DIP), approximately 744 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), approximately 306 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (DIP), two fire hydrant assemblies, 11 sanitary sewer manholes and easements, for property located at 3622 Whites Creek Pike, also known as Whites Creek Estates.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated easements have no market value according to the Department of Water and Sewerage Services.\n\n"
}
